.TH SDL_PRISZ_PREFIX 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_PRISZ_PREFIX \- A printf-formatting string prefix for a
.BR size_t
value.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_PRISZ_PREFIX \(dqz\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is just the prefix! You probably actually want
.BR SDL_PRISZu ,
.BR SDL_PRISZx ,
or
.BR SDL_PRISZX
instead\[char46]
.PP
Use it like this:

.IP
.EX
SDL_Log("There are %" SDL_PRISZ_PREFIX "u bottles of beer on the wall.", bottles);
.EE
.PP

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]6\[char46]0\[char46]

